From 25ded9c1759247e61dbdc05f2f01a0cf74857565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:17:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation: functions of a point refused only for a
 library without them

Since the functions of batches and of a point are detected independently,
a library of the generic-parallel interface built with the
generic_functions option provides both. The comments of the headers
(LibrariesManager, functions of a point and their debugging versions, C
bindings), the messages of integrate and integrate_debug, the web page
and the release notes said that the functions of a point refuse any
library of the generic-parallel interface: they now refer to a library
built without this option. The release notes describe the independent
detection, the refusal of a library without any of these functions and
the report function required by an asynchronous computation.
---
