diff --git a/docs/web/generic-parallel.md b/docs/web/generic-parallel.md
index f96ddae..26001e6 100644
--- a/docs/web/generic-parallel.md
+++ b/docs/web/generic-parallel.md
@@ -68,8 +68,11 @@ does not depend on `TFEL` at compile time.
 The functions acting on a single integration point (`integrate` on a
 `BehaviourDataView`, `integrate_debug`, the initialize functions, the
 post-processings and the rotations of a point, the `C` bindings) report an
-error for a `generic-parallel` library. Conversely, the batch functions
-report an error for a library of the `generic` interface.
+error for a library without the functions of a point, generated by the
+`generic-parallel` interface without its `generic_functions` option.
+Conversely, the batch functions report an error for a library without the
+functions of batches of points, such as a library of the `generic`
+interface.
 
 The functions of batches of points and the functions of a point are
 detected independently: the former exist if the library exports
@@ -457,7 +460,8 @@ execution context.
