-- the functions acting on a single point report an error for a
-  `generic-parallel` library instead of calling a null pointer.
+- the functions of batches of points and the functions of a point are
+  detected independently: the former if the library exports their
+  version, the latter if it exports `Generic` as interface. A library of
+  the `generic-parallel` interface built with the `generic_functions`
+  option of `MFront` contains both, and both are loaded. A library with
+  none of them is refused;
+- an asynchronous computation requires the report function of the
+  library;
+- the functions acting on a single point report an error for a library
+  without the functions of a point instead of calling a null pointer.
 
 # Layouts and views
 
